,"ui.sky.open":`Look up tonight`,"ui.sky.title":`Look up tonight`,"ui.sky.up":`{body} is up right now! Face {dir} and look about {fists} fists above the ground.`,"ui.sky.upDay":`{body} is up in the {dir}, about {fists} fists high, but the Sun is out. Look again after dark.`,"ui.sky.down":`{body} is below the ground right now. It rises at {time}.`,"ui.sky.signalMin":`{km} million km away. A radio message takes {min} minutes to get there.`,"ui.sky.signalSec":`{km} km away. A radio message takes {sec} seconds to get there.`,"ui.sky.place":`Sky as seen from {place}.`,"ui.sky.useMine":`Use my location`,"ui.sky.yourPlace":`where you are`,"ui.body.Mars":`Mars`,"ui.body.Moon":`The Moon`,"ui.dir.N":`north`,"ui.dir.NE":`north-east`,"ui.dir.E":`east`,"ui.dir.SE":`south-east`,"ui.dir.S":`south`,"ui.dir.SW":`south-west`,"ui.dir.W":`west`,"ui.dir.NW":`north-west`,"place.kandy":`Kandy, Sri Lanka`,"ui.about.what":`The Abandoned Explorers is an interactive 3D journey by Team Zorvex for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026 (Kandy, Sri Lanka). Children play the true missions of machines NASA left on the Moon and Mars, and learn the science each one made possible.`,"ui.about.sources":`6. Every fact in the stories`,"ui.about.sourcesNote":`Every line a machine speaks rests on one of these facts, each checked against the linked source.`,"ui.about.credits":`7. Code libraries (no data)`,"ui.about.ai":`How we used AI`,"ui.about.aiNote":`We used an AI coding assistant (Claude, by Anthropic) to help write code and draft text. People on the team checked every fact against the linked sources. The voices are AI-generated with the open Kokoro text-to-speech model (run on our own computer). There are no AI-generated images or models. The full log is in docs/AI_USAGE.md in our repository.`,"ui.about.disclaimer":`NASA does not endorse this project. NASA imagery and data are used under NASA's media guidelines and credited to their sources.`,"ui.subtitle":`Abandoned but not Forgotten.`,"ui.start":`Start`